### HTTP API Endpoints

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-API-ROUTING","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"SH-API-APPS","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"GET /api/v1/apps/{id} — single app status + namespace details.","impl_has":"do_GET routing uses `path.count('/') == 4` to distinguish /api/v1/apps/{id} from /api/v1/apps/{id}/logs. The path /api/v1/apps/board-manager has exactly 4 slashes. However, /api/v1/apps/board-manager/logs has 5 slashes and is caught first (the elif with endswith('/logs') comes after the count==4 check). This ordering is correct BUT the count==4 check rejects any path with more segments — so a future endpoint /api/v1/apps/{id}/something-other-than-logs would fall through to the 404 handler. More critically, the logs route check does NOT verify path.count('/') == 5, so /api/v1/apps/logs would incorrectly try to find app_id='logs'.","impl_file":"hub.py:742-769","recommendation":"Rewrite routing to split path into parts list and match by parts[4] (app_id) and parts[5] (action/subresource). Remove the count-slash heuristic. Validate parts length before indexing.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-STATUS-SHAPE","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"SH-API-STATUS","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"GET /api/v1/status apps section: {app_id: {running, container_id, image, ports, health, restart_count, exported_namespaces}}","impl_has":"ComposeAppProcess.status() returns: {id, running, container_id, container_name, image, ports, health, restart_count, exported_namespaces}. Extra field 'container_name' is not in spec. Field 'health' contains the Docker status string (e.g. 'running', 'exited') rather than the spec's 'healthy'/'unhealthy' terminology. The spec's example shows health: 'healthy' which implies a semantic health value, not the raw Docker state string.","impl_file":"hub.py:657-678","recommendation":"Add a health normalization step: map Docker state 'running' to 'healthy', 'exited'/'dead' to 'unhealthy', 'restarting' to 'restarting', etc. The 'container_name' field is additive and non-breaking — keep it but note it as an extension of the spec.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-API-DEPLOY-ASYNC","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P2","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"SH-API-APPS","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"POST /api/v1/apps/{id}/deploy — deploy or redeploy (build + start). Spec does not address synchrony.","impl_has":"POST /deploy is synchronous — the HTTP handler blocks while docker build (up to 300s) and docker run (up to 60s) complete. The HTTP client will not receive a response for potentially 5+ minutes on a cold build. No timeout on the HTTP connection from client side.","impl_file":"hub.py:802-810","recommendation":"POST /deploy should be asynchronous: spawn a background thread for build+start, return 202 Accepted with a job ID immediately. Add GET /api/v1/apps/{id}/deploy-status or rely on GET /api/v1/apps/{id} to poll. This is especially important for CI/deploy scripts that have HTTP timeouts.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-API-WORKLOAD-MGMT","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"SH-API-APPS","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"SH-ARCH lists endpoints: GET /api/v1/workloads — list workloads. Spec does not define workload management endpoints (start/stop/restart for individual workloads).","impl_has":"GET /api/v1/workloads returns all workload statuses. No POST endpoints for individual workload control. No GET /api/v1/workloads/{id} endpoint.","impl_file":"hub.py:734-736","recommendation":"Acceptable for v2 scope — spec does not require workload management endpoints. Consider adding GET /api/v1/workloads/{id} for parity with apps. Low priority.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-http_api","area":"http_api","total_gaps":4,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":2,"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED":2,"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED":0},"by_priority":{"P1":1,"P2":2,"P3":1},"notes":"The routing bug (gap-SH-API-ROUTING) is the most significant — it can misroute requests in edge cases. The synchronous deploy is an operational concern for long builds."}

