### MQTT Credential Injection

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-TRANSPORT-DEFAULT","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"mqtt_credential_injection","spec_ref":"SH-DEPLOY-TRANSPORT","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"COMPOSEIO_MQTT_BROKER sourced from app.transports[type=mqtt].broker. The spec's canonical example shows 'mqtt-broker.local'.","impl_has":"_build_transport_env() falls through to defaults 'localhost' / '1883' when no MQTT transport is declared in the config, or when the for-else fires with no MQTT transport found. A .compose.yaml without an explicit transports section gets broker=localhost injected, which will silently fail on the production machine where the broker is at mqtt-broker.local.","impl_file":"hub.py:698-701","recommendation":"Default broker should be 'mqtt-broker.local' not 'localhost', OR the hub should refuse to start a ComposeApp that has no MQTT transport declared (log ERROR and skip deploy). Silent misconfiguration is worse than a loud failure.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-SH-TRANSPORT-OVERRIDE","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"mqtt_credential_injection","spec_ref":"SH-DEPLOY-TRANSPORT","spec_file":"13-service-hub-v2.smd","spec_says":"Hub injects MQTT credentials via environment variables. Spec table shows 4 variables.","impl_has":"_build_transport_env() injects all 4 spec variables correctly. Additionally, start() adds env vars from docker.environment first, then calls _build_transport_env() and appends those — the hub's injected values appear last in the docker run command, which means they override any values in docker.environment for the same keys. This is the correct precedence (hub wins over config) and matches the comment 'override any from config to ensure correctness'.","impl_file":"hub.py:497-509","recommendation":"Behavior is correct and intentional. Spec says 'hub provisions transport credentials' which implies hub authority. Document this override behavior in the .compose.yaml spec (08) so app authors know not to hardcode COMPOSEIO_MQTT_BROKER in environment.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-mqtt_credential_injection","area":"mqtt_credential_injection","total_gaps":2,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":1,"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED":1},"by_priority":{"P2":1,"P3":1},"notes":"Injection mechanism is structurally correct. The wrong default broker is the actionable issue — it will cause silent failures on mqtt-broker.local deployments."}

