## Compliance Table

| ID | Requirement | Status | Gap |
|----|-------------|--------|-----|
| SH-C1 | Existing workloads continue unchanged | PASS | None |
| SH-C2 | ComposeApp deploys via .compose.yaml | PARTIAL | Hub reads config, but does not auto-deploy on startup (gap-SH-CAPS-AUTODEPLOY) |
| SH-C3 | MQTT credentials injected via environment | PARTIAL | Injection works, but default broker is localhost not mqtt-broker.local (gap-SH-TRANSPORT-DEFAULT) |
| SH-C4 | Port bindings from config | PASS | Ports passed to docker run -p correctly |
| SH-C5 | Volume persistence | PASS | Volumes passed to docker run -v, Docker handles persistence |
| SH-C6 | Hub API returns both tiers | PASS | GET /api/v1/status includes workloads and apps |
| SH-C7 | Container health monitoring within 10s | PARTIAL | 6s effective cycle (within 10s window), but dark-app problem (gap-SH-HEALTH-SCOPE) |
| SH-C8 | Deploy/stop/restart via API | PARTIAL | Works but stop is not idempotent (gap-SH-STOP-RUNNING-CHECK), deploy is synchronous (gap-SH-API-DEPLOY-ASYNC) |
| SH-C9 | Hub survives container crash | PARTIAL | Hub survives, but stops monitoring after first crash (gap-SH-HUB-RESTART-APPS) |
| SH-C10 | Docker restart policy honored | PARTIAL | Policy is passed to docker run, but default is 'no' not 'always' (gap-SH-RESTART-DEFAULT) |

